{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The heat shrink tubing fits a concrete use alongside my crimp connectors: insulating and protecting wiring repairs.",
    "The steel-reinforced epoxy connects with my interest in repair adhesives, although I would need a suitable repair before choosing that large pack."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The feeler gauge, threading kit, cutting wheels and wire brushes require specific tasks or compatible tools that my purchases do not establish.",
    "Water testing and electronic cleaning do not follow directly from buying clamps and connectors. Clear glue and a hundred-pack of one nut size also need a more specific reason for me to buy them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying repair supplies seems to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop tool, even when it serves a different task.",
    "My Gorilla tape purchases seem to have been treated as interest in Gorilla glue, but a shared brand does not mean the adhesive suits my next repair."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A useful connection is how an item works with supplies I already bought, such as tubing that protects connections made with my crimp terminals.",
    "Exact size, tool compatibility and quantity matter to me. My latest duct clamps do not establish a need for a particular threaded nut or a large adhesive pack."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my practical repair interests, but often assume a specific project where my history only supports a broader possibility."
}"}
